            "description": "\ufeff# Welcome to MyWorld!\r\nPackage-name is a web scraper that fetches relevant data from [nairaland](https://nairaland.com)\r\n\r\n## Installation\r\nYou can install  this package via pip using:\r\n\r\n    pip install package-name\r\n\r\n## Usage\r\nThe nairaland scraper, defines two classes - one for getting data from the homepage(**Hompage**), the other for getting data from a category(**Category**)\r\n\r\n> **Homepage**\r\n\r\nCreate a Homepage object using:\r\n\r\n    obj = Homepage()\r\nYou can optionally pass a header argument to the homepage object. The header argument will be used when making request.\r\n \r\n The Homepage class defines some method which can be used in get various data from the homepage.\r\n\r\n**Methods**\r\n\r\n    obj.get_page(url) # Returns response with the contents(bytes)\r\n    \r\n    obj.get_soup_obj(url) # Return Soup object\r\n    \r\n    obj.get_board(soup) # Return list of tuples containing link to the post and plain text of the post\r\n    \r\n    obj.get_stats(soup) # Return stats of page\r\n    \r\n    obj.get_active_members(soup) # returns active memeber\r\n\r\n\r\n> **Category**\r\n\r\nCreate a Category object using:\r\n\r\n    obj = Category()\r\nYou can optionally pass a header and category argument to the category object. The header argument will be used when making request.\r\n \r\n The Category class defines some method which can be used in get various data from various Category.\r\n\r\n**Methods**\r\n\r\n    obj.get_category() # Returns a given category url\r\n    \r\n    obj.get_soup_obj_category() # Return Soup object\r\n    \r\n    obj.get_category_post(soup) # Return list of tuples with containing title,link,author,views of a post in the specified category\r\n\r\n",
